course: dictionary
lesson: 10324
title: Traditional words and traditional ways
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Traditional means done the same way for a long time, and passed down from older people to younger people. A recipe your grandmother has used for years is a traditional recipe.
explain: It can also mean old-fashioned or usual, not new or modern. «The hongi is a traditional Maori greeting in New Zealand, done when you are invited.» The greeting is not new. People have shared it the same way for generations, and it is still done today.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Traditional bow hair is horsehair» tells you that horsehair is the usual, long-used material for bows. Try swapping in "usual, passed down" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Traditional means done the same way for a long time and passed down.
fact: Traditional also means old-fashioned or usual, not new or modern.
fact: Phrases you may meet are traditional tale, traditional dress, traditional recipe and traditional way.
fact: «Goldilocks» and «Jack and the Beanstalk» are traditional tales, also called fairy tales or folk tales.
fact: «Laozi» is the traditional author of the Dao De Jing, which means people have long said he wrote it, although some historians doubt he was one person.
exercise: «The hongi is a traditional Maori greeting in New Zealand.» What does traditional mean here? | Only for children | Brand new and modern | Very loud and busy | *Done the same way for a long time and passed down
exercise: Ava's grandma makes a traditional recipe for pancakes every year. What does traditional recipe mean? | *A recipe passed down from older people | A recipe invented yesterday | A recipe with no food in it | A recipe made by a robot
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Traditional bow hair is horsehair» that shows horsehair is the usual, long-used choice. | *traditional | hair | strings | bow
test: Which is the best meaning of traditional in «a traditional tale»? | *A story passed down through many generations | A story with no words at all | A story sent by text message | A story about the future
test: Mia asks: is traditional the same as modern? | Yes, they mean exactly the same | Traditional means very fast | Only on Tuesdays | *No, modern means new, and traditional means old-fashioned or usual
exam: In «red is just the traditional colour», what does traditional suggest? | A brand new colour | A dangerous colour | A very loud colour | *The usual colour people have always used
